# ESP32 Smart Motor Control & Environmental Monitoring using MQTT

## Overview

This project is an IoT-based system that combines environmental monitoring with remote DC motor control using an ESP32, MQTT protocol, and a BME280 sensor.

The ESP32 continuously publishes environmental data (temperature, humidity, and pressure) to an MQTT Broker while simultaneously receiving commands to control a DC motor's power, direction, and speed.

The system demonstrates bidirectional MQTT communication, making it suitable for Industrial IoT, Smart Factory, and Smart Home applications.

---

## Features

### Environmental Monitoring

- Read Temperature using BME280
- Read Humidity using BME280
- Read Atmospheric Pressure
- Publish sensor data every 5 seconds

### DC Motor Control

- Turn motor ON/OFF remotely
- Change motor direction (Forward / Reverse)
- Control motor speed using PWM (0–100%)

### MQTT Communication

Publish Topics

| Topic | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| home/esp32/sensor/temperature | Temperature (°C) |
| home/esp32/sensor/humidity | Humidity (%) |
| home/esp32/sensor/pressure | Pressure (hPa) |
| home/esp32/status/motor | Motor Status |
| home/esp32/status/direction | Current Direction |
| home/esp32/status/speed | Current Speed |

Subscribe Topics

| Topic | Payload |
|--------|----------|
| home/esp32/motor/power | ON / OFF |
| home/esp32/motor/direction | FORWARD / REVERSE |
| home/esp32/motor/speed | 0–100 |

