---

## Wiring

### BME280

| BME280 | ESP32 |
|---------|-------|
| VCC | 3.3V |
| GND | GND |
| SDA | GPIO21 |
| SCL | GPIO22 |

---

### Motor Driver (L298N)

| L298N | ESP32 |
|--------|-------|
| ENA | GPIO25 |
| IN1 | GPIO26 |
| IN2 | GPIO27 |
| GND | GND |

Power Connections

- Motor Power → External 5V Supply
- L298N GND → ESP32 GND (Common Ground)

---

## Project Architecture

```
             +----------------+
             |     MQTTX      |
             +--------+-------+
                      |
               MQTT Commands
                      |
                      |
              +-------v--------+
              |   Mosquitto    |
              | MQTT Broker    |
              +-------+--------+
                      |
        +-------------+--------------+
        |                            |
        |                            |
+-------v--------+           +--------v--------+
|     ESP32      |           |    MQTT Client  |
|                |           |   (Subscriber)  |
|  MQTT Client   |           +-----------------+
|                |
|  BME280 Sensor |
|                |
|  L298N Driver  |
|                |
|   DC Motor     |
+----------------+
```

---

## MQTT Workflow

1. ESP32 connects to WiFi.
2. ESP32 connects to Mosquitto Broker.
3. ESP32 publishes sensor readings every 5 seconds.
4. MQTT clients subscribe to sensor topics.
5. User sends motor commands through MQTTX.
6. ESP32 receives commands and controls the motor.
7. ESP32 publishes current motor status.

